[Music]  okay  so this is my spoiler free review  of cobra kai season three now i just  want to say that  i was a huge fan of karate kid as a kid  growing up  and then i hadn't watched the films in  forever they've kind of become a blur to  me  so i decided to rewatch all the films  and then i binged season one and two  recently so where i stand on all this is  that  i think that season one was amazing it  lived up to the hype and i was  really actually disappointed in season  two especially in the second half of  season two  where it became more of a teen drama  and kind of went away from focusing on  the adults of the story  and it also lost a lot of doing comedy  in it which was so well done in season  one now i'm here to tell you  because of this i kept my expectations  right in the middle  loving season one disappointing season  two i'm like okay let's see what season  three is all about  let me just say what is great about  season three  is that it fixes that huge  complaint where it really  really stays away from teen drama and  focuses back on the adults and i mean  if you're gonna look at the screen time  of season three it is mostly on  adult characters we love here and very  little on the students themselves and as  you see  what this show does so well is tying  into the original films  and justifying story lines being brought  in and characters from original films  being brought in to fit  the themes and storyline on the current  show they do it so  well in season three and as you see in  the trailer we're gonna have characters  appear from karate kid 2.  it mostly leans into karate kid 2 season  3  and i was not a fan of croticade to the  film it was my least favorite karate kid  film  yes i like the next karate kid and  karate kid 3 better than karate kid 2.  but i loved what they did with karate  kid 2  here in season 3 it made me appreciate  it more and i think actually  the story lines attached to karate kid 2  and the characters brought back  are the highlights of season 3 for me  what really works now  just with our main character in johnny  lawrence  and his growth as a character is that  as much as i didn't like the finale of  season two and i thought this whole  fight in school was a mess  it was a great catalyst for season three  because as the season starts out you're  gonna see  every character has to react to what  happened to miguel and it shakes  things up which was desperately needed  because the show is starting to feel a  little stagnant  and from that point on the pace is  really good  and they also really develop creases  character really well  and what you're going to see is it's so  well paced between  daniel johnny and chris this season with  a little drop  of the stuff with the students so that  was so effective that they went that way  and they do such a great job of it  and when i come back to how they brought  the comedy back again they lean into  that  johnny being a big kid which is great  some of his lines are just excellent  here again that make you really laugh  the comedy's not as tight as season one  but it's way better than season two's  comedy it made me laugh a lot and it  also  again the show's best when it's feel  good as well and it  does justice to that feel of the  original karate kid movies  it being a little cheesy it having a  heart and  it felt like it hit that magic again in  season three like it did in season one  which i thought was missing in season  two you're gonna see a lot of easter  eggs here  obviously i'm not gonna spoil any of  them but you're gonna be satisfied they  all really do pay off and tie  thematically  really well it's so impressive how much  effort this writing team puts in and  shows how much they really love this  franchise in the films and what's  crazy about season three is it sets up  super hype and excitement for season  four  so i will say that season three is light  years better than season two  not as good as season one but that's a  really hard task season one  is excellent so to live up to that it's  gonna be tough but it's close so  i was really happy with cobra kai season  three i think fans are gonna absolutely  love it  and if you like season two you're  probably not gonna be blown away by  season three because it's ten times  better  so i give season three an eight point  eight now i'm gonna delve into every  single episode of my spoiler review i'm  gonna break down  all my thoughts that will be coming out  when the show comes out so you're not  gonna want to miss that  please let me know down below if you  plan on watching season three what you  thought of the  original movies what you thought of  season one and two any theories you got  for season three i'd love to hear them  and just get the discussion going about  cobra kai as a whole i really want to  hear  everyone's thoughts on it please make  sure to subscribe to my channel it helps  me in so many ways like i said you're  not going to miss that big spoiler  review i'm going to have for the season  and please follow me at steve all the  show on twitter instagram for more of me  and i'll see you next time

